 Vice President (VP) — Operational Excellence
 Position Overview
 The Vice President (VP) of Operational Excellence is responsible for formulating and executing the company's overall operational excellence strategy. This role drives the optimization of operational systems and processes, Lean management, quality enhancement, cost optimization, and continuous improvement. By establishing a highly efficient, standardized, and digitalized operational management system, the VP continuously improves operational efficiency, product quality, and supply chain collaboration capabilities, ensuring sustained growth and enhancing the company's overall competitiveness in the global jewelry market.
 Key Responsibilities
 I. Operational Excellence Strategy and System Development
 Formulate the company's medium- to long-term operational excellence strategy and implementation plan;
 Establish and continuously optimize the operational excellence management system;
 Drive Lean manufacturing, Continuous Improvement initiatives, and the standardization of operations.
 II. Operational Optimization and Process Improvement
 Continuously optimize production, supply chain, and operational processes;
 Drive cross-departmental process integration to enhance overall operational efficiency;
 Establish Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) and operational management guidelines.
 III. Quality and Performance Management
 Establish and refine quality management and operational performance management systems;
 Drive continuous product quality improvement and mitigate quality risks;
 Define operational KPIs and continuously enhance overall operational performance.
 IV. Cross-departmental Collaboration and Operational Management
 Coordinate across departments such as production, supply chain, procurement, quality, logistics, and sales;
 Ensure operational goals align with the company's overall strategy;
 Foster efficient collaboration among departments to boost overall operational capabilities.
 V. Continuous Improvement and Digital Transformation
 Utilize operational excellence tools (e.g., Lean, Six Sigma) to drive continuous improvement;
 Implement digital operations and smart manufacturing projects;
 Optimize operational efficiency, costs, and resource allocation through data analysis.
 VI. Risk and Compliance Management
 Identify potential risks within operational management processes;
 Ensure production operations comply with relevant laws, regulations, industry standards, and customer requirements;
 Establish robust risk control mechanisms to ensure the company's sustained, stable, and efficient operation. Qualifications
 20–25 years of experience in operations management, operational excellence, supply chain, or related fields;
 Over 8 years of experience in senior management roles (Director level or above);
 Familiarity with production operations, supply chain, and quality management systems in the jewelry or luxury goods industry is preferred;
 Experience in international manufacturing operations or global supply chain management is preferred;
 Familiarity with operational excellence tools and systems—such as Lean, Six Sigma, Continuous Improvement (CI), ERP, and MES—is preferred;
 Possesses outstanding strategic thinking, organizational and coordination skills, leadership capabilities, and execution prowess.
 We Offer
 Competitive executive compensation and benefits packages;
 Long-term career development and advancement opportunities;
 The opportunity to serve as a core management team member of a rapidly growing international jewelry enterprise;
 - The chance to play a key role in formulating and implementing the company's global operational excellence strategy.
